uage":"en","link":[{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/aip\/apl\/article-pdf\/70\/10\/1296\/18525327\/1296_1_online.pdf","content-type":"application\/pdf","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"syndication"},{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/aip\/apl\/article-pdf\/70\/10\/1296\/18525327\/1296_1_online.pdf","content-type":"unspecified","content-version":"vor","intended-application":"similarity-checking"}],"deposited":{"date-parts":[[2024,2,3]],"date-time":"2024-02-03T12:19:56Z","timestamp":1706962796000},"score":107.19713,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/pubs.aip.org\/apl\/article\/70\/10\/1296\/532254\/Transmission-electron-holography-of-silicon"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1997,3,10]]},"references-count":24,"journal-issue":{"issue":"10","published-print":{"date-parts":[[1997,3,10]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/1.118556","ISSN":["0003-6951","1077-3118"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0003-6951","type":"print"},{"value":"1077-3118","type":"electronic"}],"published-other":{"date-parts":[[1997,3,10]]},"published":{"date-parts":[[1997,3,10]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2024,9,10]],"date-time":"2024-09-10T00:07:05Z","timestamp":1725926825961},"reference-count":10,"publisher":"Oxford University Press (OUP)","issue":"S2","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[1997,8,1]],"date-time":"1997-08-01T00:00:00Z","timestamp":870393600000},"content-version":"vor","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/academic.oup.com\/journals\/pages\/open_access\/funder_policies\/chorus\/standard_publication_model"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1997,8,1]]},"abstract":"<jats:title>Abstract<\/jats:title>\n               <jats:p>The phase shift imparted to an incident high-energy electron wave in a TEM is related to the specimen\u2019s electron-refractive properties. These, in turn, are related to the electrostatic potential and, by Fourier transform (1), to the electron scattering factors fe \u00a0i(s) for the various atom species i in the specimen and scattering vectors s. The average refractive index is determined by the mean electrostatic (inner) potential, \u03a6o, and can be modelled as \u03a6o = (C\/\u03a9) \u03a3fe \u00a0i(s0) [equation 1] where C = 47.878 (V-\u00c52) and the summation runs over all of the atoms in the unit volume \u03a9 (2). Calculated fe \u00a0i(s) data are available from the literature (e.g. 3). These calculations have only been done for neutral atoms and some fully ionized cations and anions. They do not account for electron redistribution due to covalent bonding to which \u03a6o is quite sensitive (4).<\/jats:p>\n               <jats:p>This research is making \u03a6o measurements using transmission electron holography. Holograms were collected using a 200keV Philips CM20 FEG TEM equipped with a non-rotatable biprism (5) and a Gatan 794 Multiscan camera.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1017\/s1431927600012162","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2020,7,2]],"date-time":"2020-07-02T08:37:55Z","timestamp":1593679075000},"page":"1055-1056","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["Electron Refraction of Amorphous Nanospheres"],"prefix":"10.1093","volume":"3","author":[{"given":"YC","family":"Wang","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Stevens Institute of Technology , Hoboken, New Jersey, 07030"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"TM","family":"Chou","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Stevens Institute of Technology , Hoboken, New Jersey, 07030"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]},{"given":"M","family":"Libera","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Stevens Institute of Technology , Hoboken, New Jersey, 07030"}],"role":[{"role":"author","vocabulary":"crossref"}]}],"member":"286","published-online":{"date-parts":[[1997,8,1]]},"reference":[{"volume-title":"International Tables for X-ray Crystallography","year":"1992","author":"Wilson","key":"2024090915335889500_ref1"},{"key":"202