5","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"481","DOI":"10.1107\/S0108767393013200","volume":"A50","author":"Rez","year":"1994","journal-title":"Acta Cryst."},{"key":"10.1016\/B978-044482051-8\/50023-3_bib6","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"285","DOI":"10.1016\/0304-3991(93)90197-6","volume":"50","author":"Gajdardziska-Josifovska","year":"1993","journal-title":"Ultramicroscopy"},{"key":"10.1016\/B978-044482051-8\/50023-3_bib7","volume":"Vol. III","year":"1968"},{"key":"10.1016\/B978-044482051-8\/50023-3_bib8","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1","DOI":"10.1016\/0304-3991(93)90130-P","volume":"51","author":"Joy","year":"1993","journal-title":"Ultramicroscopy"},{"key":"10.1016\/B978-044482051-8\/50023-3_bib9","unstructured":"Image version 1.45, public-domain software (Macintosh) available from the National Institute of Health"},{"key":"10.1016\/B978-044482051-8\/50023-3_bib10","series-title":"Proc. 52nd Annual Meeting of MSA","first-page":"444","author":"Libera","year":"1994"}],"container-title":["Electron Holography"],"language":"en","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2019,1,6]],"date-time":"2019-01-06T14:54:39Z","timestamp":1546786479000},"score":47.087868,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/linkinghub.elsevier.com\/retrieve\/pii\/B9780444820518500233"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[1995]]},"ISBN":["9780444820518"],"references-count":10,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1016\/b978-044482051-8\/50023-3","published":{"date-parts":[[1995]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,9,1]],"date-time":"2026-09-01T15:07:20Z","timestamp":1788275240382,"version":"build-2803163510"},"reference-count":8,"publisher":"AIP Publishing","issue":"7","content-domain":{"domain":["pubs.aip.org"],"crossmark-restriction":true},"published-print":{"date-parts":[[1997,2,17]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>We have demonstrated a room-temperature silicon single-electron transistor memory that consists of (i) a narrow channel metal-oxide\u2013semiconductor field-effect transistor with a width (\u223c10 nm) smaller than the Debye screening length of single electron; and (ii) a nanoscale polysilicon dot (\u223c7\u00d77 nm) as the floating gate embedded between the channel and the control gate. We have observed that storing one electron on the floating gate can significantly screen the channel from the potential on the control gate, leading to a discrete shift in the threshold voltage, a staircase relationship between the charging voltage and the threshold shift, and a self-limiting charging process.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.1063\/1.118236","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2002,7,26]],"date-time":"2002-07-26T13:36:08Z","timestamp":1027690568000},"page":"850-852","update-policy":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.1063\/aip-crossmark-policy-page","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":127,"title":["A room-temperature silicon single-electron metal\u2013oxide\u2013semiconductor memory with nanoscale floating-gate and ultranarrow channel"],"prefix":"10.1063","volume":"70","author":[{"given":"Lingjie","family":"Guo","sequence":"first","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, NanoStructure Laboratory, University of Minnesota, Minneapolis, Minnesota 55455"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Effendi","family":"Leobandung","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, NanoStructure Laboratory, University of Minnesota, Minneapolis, Minnesota 55455"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]},{"given":"Stephen Y.","family":"Chou","sequence":"additional","affiliation":[{"name":"Department of Electrical Engineering, NanoStructure Laboratory, University of Minnesota, Minneapolis, Minnesota 55455"}],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"317","reference":[{"key":"2024020312164094000_r1","doi-asserted-by":"crossref","first-page":"1628","DOI":"10.1109\/16.310117","volume":"41","year":"1994","journal-title":"IEEE Trans. Electron Devices"},{"key":"20240203